{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And my people are suspended</b> — with alef, like תלאום (they would hang them). And the yod in למשובתי is not a sign of the verb, like ושימחתים, בית תפלתי, אשתחוה אל היכל קדשך ביראתך. For משובה is always pejorative. And the meaning is that they practice the way of backsliding: my people is like a man suspended in the air, neither rising upward nor descending downward." "<b>And El Most High</b> — like נאם הגבר הוקם על, which is an epithet like עליון. And its meaning is: the callers call Him El Most High — and they are the prophets of HaShem — and all follow one path: לא ירימו ראש."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra cites multiple scriptural forms to illustrate that the yod in למשובתי is nominal rather than verbal; the four Hebrew strings are quoted in sequence without explicit separators in the source.", 1 "Resolved הם נביאי השם as referring to הקוראים; the subject of לא ירימו ראש (from Exodus 30:32) is elliptical, rendered literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:01.770939641Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}